  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=106",
      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Otocinclus mariae Fowler, 1940</li><li>Size: 33 mm (1.3\") SL</li><li>Identification: very similar to O. vittatus.</li><li>Peaceful.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=106",
      "html": "<p>South America: Upper Madeira and lower Amazon River basins. Type locality: Boca Chapare, Río Chimore, tributary to Río Ichilo, Río Mamoré system, Bolivia. IUCN Red List: Least Concern (assessed 2020).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=106",
      "html": "<ul><li>pH: 5.5–7.5</li><li>Temperature: 21–26°C (69.8–78.8°F)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=106",
      "html": "<p>Large-leafed plants and vertical flat rock surfaces (especially slate). Not essential, but it likes bogwood and a large rounded substrate. Live plants seem essential to the long-term survival of this fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=106",
      "html": "<p>Initially algae: add a shoal to an \"algaefied\" tank and then supplement the diet with sinking tablets and the usual cucumber, lettuce or courgette (zucchini).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=106",
      "html": "<p>Peaceful. Keep in groups (preferably at least six) with any small to mid-sized community fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=106",
      "html": "<p>Females are larger and broader, especially when viewed from above.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=106",
      "html": "<p>There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=106",
      "html": "<p>Proceedings of the Academy of Natural Sciences of Philadelphia v. 92, pp 83, Figs. 41-43.</p>"
    }
